  "description": "Before she knew it, Irene found herself married to Felix, whom she had secretly admired from afar, by royal decree. Although it was a marriage of convenience, Felix treated her with great respect, and Irene was very happy with the marriage. She was convinced that they would continue to be happy together.\n\n *“Do you know that the Duke is having an affair, Duchess?”*\n\nThat is, until a paparazzo showed up and presented her with photos he’d secretly taken of Felix with another woman... \n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
